    10	- The identity experiment stopped before its first call: a proposed success label would merge “financing actually provided in 2026” into “guarantee amount.” Reading the full answer ranges disproved that label. The error is already in extraction call 460 and appears in three saved runs. Two other Ohio splits did have their relevant old theses in the search list. Source context remains a hypothesis, not a proved fix; no model experiment or default grouping integration occurred.
    11	- D158 [root-cause trace](../poc/reports/2026-10-25-ohio-grouping-02/results.md) remains relevant: missing questions and wrong relations are already present in extraction. The implementation's numeric-first and official-date restrictions are narrower than the PRD; its question-first role remains an unvalidated experiment, not the default. The previously proposed automatic continuation of that comparison is superseded by D159's full-path diagnosis.
    12	- Confirmed code defect fixed: the next-year numeric limit no longer rejects explicit event/policy_event candidates. Replaying all 326 stored answers (172 candidates) changes exactly one NAVER deployment case: one question and three evidence items restored; Ohio unchanged. Eleven targeted tests, two scratch mutants, and the full 211-test Python suite pass.
    13	- Online D158 comparison is incomplete: its first control request timed out after 180.342 seconds with no response. One attempt, $0.105535 reservation retained because server-side usage is unknown; all other sequences unstarted. No fresh semantic result, no automatic resend, no default grouping integration. Inputs, requests, logs and hashes are preserved.
    14	- D157 remains a failed business acceptance: 20 calls, estimated $0.373923; only one of three grouping samples retained project risk and still had wrong relations. Its legal group-ID schema omission was corrected for both D158 arms; five correctly preserved bindings do not prove semantic reliability.
    15	- Completed D156: the [grouping acceptance definition](research/2026-10-25-grouping-acceptance.md) and offline checker are corrected. The four saved development runs report zero exercised new memberships; six old holdout runs remain not started. [Results](../poc/reports/2026-10-25-grouping-acceptance-01/results.md). This artifact audit did not establish semantic acceptance.
    16	- Completed Step B (D155): [grouping improvement plan](poc/grouping-improvement-plan.md). Reference lists no longer veto candidates; exact scope and full-year handling, event identity, same-answer coalescing, legacy-key trust and atomic write/resume are corrected. `poc-v16` / `role-v5` is the explicit configuration; grouping is not enabled.
