   759	- Decides:
   760	  - A view is one question, a ladder of five fixed rungs and a due date, never rewritten. It looks at one number (which
   761	    year, whether a period amount or a point-in-time value, and the source it is answered from) or the state of one
   762	    thing (scope and stage). An object view's identity is its object plus what it looks at; a theme view's identity is
   763	    only what it looks at (the theme is where it is filed), so theme views are compared across all themes. A view looks
   764	    at one thing: a question that needs a number and an event is two views joined by a dependency; a question whose
   765	    parts can move in opposite directions is two views, joined only if one really depends on the other.
   766	  - Object views (companies, crypto, commodities) have the rungs strongly bullish to strongly bearish, meaning good or
   767	    bad for the business, fixed at creation. Theme views have five outcomes on one axis, named by outcome, with no
   768	    bull or bear; each dependent object view's arrow says which end is bullish for it. The stance on the price is our
   769	    state against the consensus, which is not designed yet.
