   771	    the due date; there is no "partial". A number ladder is ranges of one number in its stated year, judged by code;
   772	    an event ladder is the states one thing can be in on the due date, judged by the model from "happened" evidence
   773	    only, citing it. The model sets the rungs when the view is created; they do not change before the due date.
   774	  - The due date is when the debate is settled, usually 6–12 months out; a number's due date is the day it is
   775	    published; quarterly reports in between are evidence. Number views carry their year (fiscal year for companies,
   776	    calendar year otherwise) and at most this year's and next year's are open at once. The year counts from the latest
   777	    publication day among the items processed so far, which only moves forward (never the wall clock); a year whose
